From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orbis-win <orbis-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: name the thread alloc_tls_slot skips

The skip leaves a thread without a TLS block for a newly loaded module, which
looked like a candidate for Wwise's threads dying. Measured 2026-11-16: it
reports tid=00d8 teb=0000000000000000, i.e. a thread the loader has not set up
yet, which allocates its own TLS later. The skip is BENIGN -- recorded so it is
not chased again.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -1374,7 +1374,15 @@
         thread = next;
         if (NtQueryInformationThread( thread, ThreadBasicInformation, &tbi, sizeof(tbi), NULL ) || !tbi.TebBaseAddress)
         {
-            ERR( "NtQueryInformationThread failed.\n" );
+            /* PW: which thread, and was a TEB simply absent? A skip here leaves
+             * that thread WITHOUT a TLS block for this module. Risk of Rain 2
+             * loads AkSoundEngine (Wwise) as a plugin after its threads exist,
+             * starts 4 audio threads, and all 4 are gone by the time the main
+             * thread parks forever in WaitForSingleObject inside Wwise. The
+             * wineserver is a thread of this process, so a TEB-less skip may be
+             * benign -- this says which it is. */
+            ERR( "NtQueryInformationThread failed. tid=%04x teb=%p\n",
+                 (unsigned int)(ULONG_PTR)tbi.ClientId.UniqueThread, tbi.TebBaseAddress );
             continue;
         }
         teb = tbi.TebBaseAddress;
